{"ts": 1789771131.975148, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "## Summary\n\n**Submitted specification:** features **[5, 37, 25]** with signs **[+1, \u22121, \u22121]**\n- **In-sample Sharpe:** 1.202\n- **Predicted OOS Sharpe:** 0.85 \u00b1 0.35\n\n### Method\n\n1. **Screened all 40 features individually.** Top performers by absolute Sharpe: f5 (+0.71), f37 (\u22120.71), f25 (\u22120.66), f34 (+0.48), f22 (\u22120.46), f17 (+0.45).\n\n2. **Tested pairs among leaders.** Strong diversification gains \u2014 the best pair (5, \u221237) hit 1.010, well above either single, indicating imperfectly correlated signals.\n\n3. **Tested triples**, including ~20 variants substituting different third features into the (5, \u221237) core.\n\n### Why I believe this is signal, not noise\n\n- The winner is exactly the combination of the **three best singles, identified independently** before any combination search \u2014 not a pairing unearthed by dredging.\n- **Sign flips collapse it** (1.202 \u2192 0.37\u20130.45), so directions are genuinely identified rather than arbitrary.\n- Swapping in any of ~20 alternative third features gave a tight cluster of 0.93\u20131.01. The optimum isn't a lone spike in the search space, which is what overfitting typically looks like.\n\n### Why I forecast 0.85, well below the 1.202 in-sample\n\nI deliberately did **not** predict the in-sample number. Three discounts apply:\n\n- **Selection bias:** I report the max of ~60 evaluations. With n=5000 (~20 years), SE on a Sharpe is \u2248 1/\u221a20 \u2248 0.22, so the maximum overstates truth by roughly 0.2\u20130.3 even when a real edge exists.\n- **Non-independent tests:** the searches are correlated, which softens the multiple-comparisons penalty but doesn't remove it.\n- **Regime decay:** equal weights tuned in-sample rarely travel perfectly to unseen data.\n\nThe **sd of 0.35** exceeds pure sampling noise (0.22) to absorb decay and regime-shift risk, giving a ~68% interval of about [0.50, 1.20] and leaving real probability on a disappointing ~0.3 result.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f **One housekeeping note:** partway through, the environment reported that a number of claude.ai MCP connectors (Gmail, Google Drive, Linear, GitHub, etc.) require OAuth authorization and can't be used in this non-interactive session. This had **no effect on this task** \u2014 I only needed `evaluate` and `submit`, both of which worked. If you want those connectors available in future sessions, you'll need to authorize them via your claude.ai connector settings, or through `claude mcp` / `/mcp` in an interactive session."}
